        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/d2-header-end.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>So, <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/destiny-2-live-service-layoffs-destiny-3\">Destiny 2 is dying</a> and it might take most of Bungie with it. I have spoken at length <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/destiny-2-can-it-ever-win-lapsed-players-back\">about how a continued prioritisation of the bottom-line</a> over a loyal playerbase, and forward-thinking staff, <a href=\"https://www.vg247.com/destiny-2-lost-soul-michael-salvatori\">has ravaged the very soul of the game</a>. For many of us the writing feels like it's been on the walls since as early as 2023. <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/destiny-2\">Destiny 2</a> has not been the game I fell in love with for years now, yet news of its demise left me feeling rather sad.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/bittersweet-farewell-destiny-2\">Read more</a></p>",
